From e191dfcd0f6c2751543fe9c94010baa224cbd257 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jan Forst <ensonador@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 19:48:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] usb.c: interface order, an optional IAD, a serial, and the
 descriptor test

FELUCCA_UAC_AC_COLLECT moves MIDI out of the AC header's collection; FELUCCA_UAC_MIDI_LAST puts
the MIDI function after the streaming interfaces (AC, AS, MIDI) instead of between them. The
fm-1-experiments bisection of #67 on macOS 15 found the ordering is what makes the audio input
enumerate; Dinghy's platform carries SLOOP before its AS-first collection change, so both are in.

FELUCCA_UAC_IAD (off by default) gives the plain build the audio function's IAD and the misc/IAD
device class. Descriptor hygiene, not a host fix: it needs FELUCCA_UAC_MIDI_LAST so the interfaces it
names (AC + AS) stay contiguous, with MIDI outside them.

FELUCCA_USB_SERIAL (default: FELUCCA_ID) gives the device a serial number string, so a host tells
firmwares sharing VID/PID 1209:0001 apart; the update loader keeps iSerialNumber 0. bcdDevice gets a
bit per layout flag. The runtime menu USB SERIAL path (FELUCCA_CDC=1) keeps its own descriptors: the
layout flags are a compile error with CDC, as build-dinghy.sh builds without it.

build.py forwards the new flags (the env settings build-dinghy.sh exports).
tests/usb_compat_test.c checks the shipped set in three variants; tests/run_tests.sh runs them.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
