  * 12 taps a phase, Q15, Felucca's 24 x Q30 made smaller) into the ring. 44.1 kHz, the rate until a host asks
- * for another, sends the samples as before, bit for bit. */
+ * for another, sends the samples as before, bit for bit.
+ * FELUCCA_UAC_AC_COLLECT=1 / FELUCCA_UAC_MIDI_LAST=1 (plain builds, FELUCCA_UAC only): the AC header's
+ * collection stops naming MIDI, and the MIDI function moves behind the streaming interfaces
+ * (AC, AS, MIDI) instead of between them: the fm-1-experiments bisection of #67 (macOS 13-15).
+ * FELUCCA_UAC_IAD=1 (plain builds): the audio function gets an IAD and the misc/IAD device class, so a
+ * host sees AC + AS as one function; needs MIDI_LAST to keep them contiguous.
+ * FELUCCA_USB_SERIAL (default FELUCCA_ID): the device's own serial number string, so a host tells
